<doxygen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="compound.xsd" version="1.18.0" xml:lang="en-US">
  <compounddef id="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-test-case" kind="group">
    <compoundname>micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-test-case</compoundname>
    <title>Test Cases</title>
    <innerclass refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case" prot="public">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::test_case</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Test cases are named sequences of checks. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A test case is created with <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput>, called on a suite, with a name and a callable, usually a lambda that receives the test case (<computeroutput>[] (auto&amp; t) { ... }</computeroutput>), followed by any arguments for the callable. The test case runs immediately, within the call, and its checks are made on the test case received by the lambda (<computeroutput>t.expect (...)</computeroutput>).</para>
<para>Write one test case for each behaviour of the code under test; the report shows the result of each test case, so a failure points to the behaviour that broke.</para>
<para>A test case can contain other test cases, created with <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput> on the test case itself (<computeroutput>t.test (...)</computeroutput>); they are reported nested.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref>;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>In<sp/>main(),<sp/>after<sp/>tr.add_top_suite():</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Check<sp/>various<sp/>conditions&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>42))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;answer<sp/>eq<sp/>42&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::ne<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>43))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;answer<sp/>ne<sp/>43&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Test cases for several values</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<computeroutput>test_each()</computeroutput>, called on a suite or on a test case, creates and runs a test case for each value of a range (a container, an array, a span, or a view), of a list written in place, or of a tuple, whose values may have different types. The callable receives the test case and the value, and a generic lambda is needed for a tuple. Each test case is named after the common name, followed by the value in parentheses, such as <computeroutput>Sizes (16)</computeroutput>; a value that cannot be written, such as an application type without an <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput>, is replaced by its position, starting at 1, such as <computeroutput>Records (#2)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref>;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test_each<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Sizes&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>16,<sp/>512<sp/>},</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>size)<sp/>{<sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::gt<sp/>(size,<sp/>0));<sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test_each<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Limits&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>{<sp/>3,<sp/>4<sp/>},</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>limit)<sp/>{<sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::gt<sp/>(limit,<sp/>2));<sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test_each<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Types&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>std::tuple{<sp/>42,<sp/>1.5,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;text&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>},</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>value)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(value,<sp/>value));</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>With the TAP reporter, the first call is reported as:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".console"><codeline><highlight class="normal">ok<sp/>1<sp/>-<sp/>Sizes<sp/>(1)<sp/>#<sp/>{<sp/>passed,<sp/>1<sp/>check<sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ok<sp/>2<sp/>-<sp/>Sizes<sp/>(16)<sp/>#<sp/>{<sp/>passed,<sp/>1<sp/>check<sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ok<sp/>3<sp/>-<sp/>Sizes<sp/>(512)<sp/>#<sp/>{<sp/>passed,<sp/>1<sp/>check<sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting>  </para>
    </detaileddescription>
  </compounddef>
